msgid ""
"Use GWexpy time helpers safely for GPS and UTC conversion, including to_gps,"
" from_gps, tconvert, LIGOTimeGPS, vectorized inputs, and timezone edge "
"cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:7 49f6e0984ad046aea8e0a0abae23497a
msgid "GPS Time Utility Functions (`gwexpy.time`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:9 5e8070d775984c21806c9611bcf2dacc
msgid ""
"`gwexpy` extends GWpy's time utilities to support vector operations on "
"pandas Series, NumPy ndarrays, and Astropy Time objects, in addition to "
"standard string/datetime scalars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:16 517bdc53e2d14279ae92b233c5f35b34
msgid "Quick Guide: Important Considerations (FAQ)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:18 1a492ad28c3246c79543977fc6c9b1e2
msgid ""
"It is important to understand these fundamental behaviors before performing "
"conversions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:20 19ba4466bb404ec6b5aa3fcc6afcc6bf
msgid "Handling Leap Seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:21 9221632f0060478f808eb43566cb6b12
msgid ""
"**GPS Time**: Continuous seconds starting from 1980-01-06 00:00:00 UTC. It "
"does not include leap seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:22 23e53dff79284b68ae8c9ba070516926
msgid ""
"**Conversion**: When converting to/from UTC, `astropy.time`'s IERS leap "
"second tables are automatically applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:23 3cc4f69061ed4e0db5ae8e928e86690d
msgid ""
"**Note**: For future dates or very recent leap seconds, you may need to "
"update `astropy` data or use the latest IERS table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:25 12253fa5c8af4393a6f971eabf992190
msgid "Strings Without Timezones"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:26 6a1ef1743b0142d597dc604d34789ab9
msgid ""
"Strings like `\"2015-09-14 09:50:45\"` without a timezone are treated as "
"**UTC by default** in `to_gps` and `tconvert`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:27 3c02d0d465b643a8a643f2169c0cc691
msgid ""
"For reliable local time conversion, always include the timezone name (e.g., "
"`\"Asia/Tokyo\"`) or provide a timezone-aware `datetime` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:29 46dfe6eb08e749d588446d7a904182f8
msgid "Common Failure Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:30 d8c11722a13b4f2ea42cbd7b4f0af91c
msgid ""
"Strings that cannot be parsed as datetimes, such as `to_gps(\"not-a-time\")`"
" or `tconvert(\"not-a-time\")`, fail with `ValueError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:31 e39088e8705847e189660dbb3d96bb12
msgid ""
"Inputs that cannot be converted to numeric GPS seconds, such as "
"`from_gps(\"abc\")`, fail with `ValueError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:32 5e07f37547cf4d3ab6cfc9e70f01c62d
msgid ""
"Unsupported keyword arguments such as `to_gps(..., timezone=\"Asia/Tokyo\")`"
" raise `TypeError` in the current implementation. Pass the timezone in the "
"string itself or use a timezone-aware `datetime`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:33 4dc86f5672cc46e79ccff57117d8a9cd
msgid ""
"Naive `datetime` inputs are treated as UTC. If you mean a local civil time, "
"use a timezone-aware `datetime`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/time_utilities.md:34 3852c3de5848442aadaf526d197b0caf
msgid ""
"For DST boundaries or other ambiguous local civil times, this page does not "
"guarantee automatic resolution. Prefer explicit UTC offsets or timezone-"
"aware `datetime` objects for boundary cases."
msgstr ""

